& [Requirements]
  + [CPBW-001] bind execution to the canonical repository root published ancestor commit and exact Cargo.lock
  + [CPBW-002] build cantor cantor-corpus cantord and cantorctl release binaries with locked offline dependencies or verify exact caller-selected prebuilt binaries from that workspace
  + [CPBW-003] require an absent absolute disposable run root whose leaf is a closed workflow-owned identity and refuse repository home drive-root traversal alias and preexisting targets
  + [CPBW-004] copy exactly four regular release binaries into the disposable bin directory and record source and installed byte and SHA256 equality
  + [CPBW-005] create two distinct fresh 32-byte fixture signing seeds only inside the disposable run root and never report their bytes
  + [CPBW-006] compile the tracked three-source self-hosted corpus with the installed cantor-corpus binary and verify the exact generated build manifest environment and query artifacts
  + [CPBW-007] initialize a strict IPv4-loopback resident-service configuration inside the disposable run root using the generated environment
  + [CPBW-008] start only the installed cantord with the installed cantorctl through the existing supervised lifecycle and require authenticated readiness
  + [CPBW-009] require fresh authenticated health to match the started PID generation activation sequence installed server and installed client identities
  + [CPBW-010] execute generated query-cantor through installed cantorctl and require a successful exact protocol result bound to the health generation
  + [CPBW-011] gracefully stop the exact generation and require process exit state removal and zero force-kill
  + [CPBW-012] after stop execute the same query through installed direct cantor and require its ProtocolResponse to equal the service nested ProtocolResponse
  + [CPBW-013] remove only the exact validated disposable run root after success and prove it absent before publishing the report
  + [CPBW-014] publish the report outside the disposable run root with exact release artifact identities step dispositions response digests rollback state and capability denials
  + [CPBW-015] on fault stop only a supervisor-state-proven matching process; if safe stop cannot be proved retain the run root and report the residual instead of deleting
  + [CPBW-016] independently verify the report against current published source artifacts and refuse unknown fields hash drift false success missing steps response mismatch residual process false rollback or stronger capability claims
  + [CPBW-017] adversarially cover unsafe roots preexisting roots nonloopback address duplicate installed identity tampered artifact false step response and rollback evidence and unknown fields
  + [CPBW-018] pass focused workflow verifier debug release warnings-denied Clippy format recursive evidence attribution commit push and post-push gates
  + [CPBW-019] never download install dependencies contact a provider use remote fallback persist service state beyond the run create production secrets effects FPGA or Minecraft scope

